    {
      "id": "7001c790-efe4-4c75-85b9-498cd585e818",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        368,
        720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 800,
        "content": "## People Search — Searchbug API\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow starts with a form where a user enters people-search criteria. It maps the submitted values into API parameters, calls the Searchbug People Search API, flattens the response, and saves the results to Google Sheets.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the People Search Form fields so they collect the required search inputs, such as first name, last name, middle name, and city.\n- Add the required Searchbug API credentials or API key in the HTTP Request node and confirm the endpoint and query parameters match your Searchbug account requirements.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials in n8n and select the target spreadsheet, sheet, and column mapping for the saved results.\n- Run a test submission to verify the API response is flattened correctly and appended to the sheet.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the form fields and Set node mappings to include additional Searchbug search parameters, modify the custom code to flatten different response fields, or change the Google Sheets destination and column layout."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
